  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1....Quiet through Thursday with high pressure in \ncontrol. \n\nHigh pressure centered west of the area this afternoon\nwill build into the region through tonight and remain centered \nnearby through Tuesday. This will bring mainly clear skies and \ntranquil weather through Tuesday and beyond. \n\nFor tonight, the combination of diminishing winds and a mainly clear \nsky will result in lows getting down into the 50s for most with even \nsome 40s possible over portions of our northeast PA zones into NW \nNJ. A sunny day will follow for Tuesday with light east winds as the \nhigh starts to move offshore. Expect highs mainly in the middle to \nupper 70s with 60s to low 70s over the Poconos into NW NJ. Humidity \nlevels will remain comfortable. \n\nBy Wednesday, temperatures climb into above normal temperatures with \nhighs in the low to mid 80s. This stretch of above normal \ntemperatures should continue until Friday with increasing levels of \nhumidity through the period. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Somewhat unsettled weather will be possible at times \nlate this week and next weekend as multiple systems move through. \nHowever at this point significant impacts due not appear likely. \n\nA cold front still looks to move southward through the area Thursday \nnight into Friday and this could result in a few showers. However, \nguidance has backed off on coverage of showers and now the end of \nthe week looks to overall remain mainly quiet for most. \n\nLooking ahead to the weekend, the aformentioned front may try \nto push back northward as a warm front by late Saturday followed\nby another cold front Sunday as low pressure moves by north of \nthe area. This will bring additional chances for showers and \nperhaps a few storms with the highest probability for \nprecipitation looking to be overnight Saturday night and \nSunday. At this point confidence is low regarding any potential \nimpacts but details will come into focus over the coming days.",
